# Extract — API Surface — <system-name>

<!--
Phase 4 output of system-dissector. Catalogues the *external* API surface
of the target system — endpoints, RPCs, webhooks, SDKs the system calls
out to, and authentication/transport mechanisms.

Goal: give `neodoo-integrate` (Phase 5, OPT-IN) the contract information
to map each endpoint to a downstream equivalent (or to a wrap/extract-pattern
strategy when no equivalent exists). Phase 5 HANDOFF é stack-agnostic e
não depende deste output.

Filling conventions:
- Group by *direction*: outbound (system calls external), inbound (system
  exposes), peer-to-peer.
- One row per endpoint. Headers / payloads summarised, not dumped.
- For each row, name a `port_strategy`: reference | wrap | extract-pattern
  | drop-in | source-port. (See `neodoo-integrate/SKILL.md` § Porting
  patterns.)
- The YAML block at the bottom is the machine-readable form `neodoo-integrate`
  parses; the table above is the human-readable index.
-->

## Como usar este documento

- **Audience**: integrador + dev backend que vai escrever adapters (stack-agnostic).
- **Next action**: ler §1 (outbound) primeiro — APIs que o sistema-alvo CONSOME informam quais licenças/deps vão entrar no ecossistema.
- **Quando re-verificar**: a cada release maior do sistema-alvo, ou quando `extract/dependencies.md` mudar.

## Evidence

- **Overall status**: `verified` | `estimated` | `mixed` *(pick one)*
- **Probe commands**: `<e.g. rg "axios|fetch|requests.post" repo/, OpenAPI export, pcap analysis>` [verified|estimated]
- **Last audit**: `<YYYY-MM-DD>`

